From 36592d4a60da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chunhai Guo
Date: Mon Mar 17 04:16:24 2025 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs: fix missing discard for active segments

UPSTREAM: f2fs: fix missing discard for active segments

add_discard_addrs() skipped any segment with 0 valid blocks, including
the current segment being trimmed at checkpoint. No discard_cmd was
created for it, yet its ckpt/cur valid maps were synced, so the missing
discard bits were never recovered and discard_blks stayed non-zero.

Only skip a 0-valid-block segment when it is not the segment currently
being trimmed.

Source: AOSP android14-6.1-lts 36592d4a60da
---
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/segment.c b/fs/f2fs/segment.c
index bd0fbc8..e5cf500 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/segment.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/segment.c
@@ -1982,7 +1982,9 @@ static bool add_discard_addrs(struct f2fs_sb_info *sbi, struct cp_control *cpc,
 		return false;
 
 	if (!force) {
-		if (!f2fs_realtime_discard_enable(sbi) || !se->valid_blocks ||
+		if (!f2fs_realtime_discard_enable(sbi) ||
+			(!se->valid_blocks &&
+				!IS_CURSEG(sbi, cpc->trim_start)) ||
 			SM_I(sbi)->dcc_info->nr_discards >=
 				SM_I(sbi)->dcc_info->max_discards)
 			return false;
